{:adr/id "2607142230"
 :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-0312 (Freshwater fishing) fleet-operations-coordination actor"
 :adr/status :accepted
 :adr/date "2026-07-14"
 :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :adr/related ["ADR-2607151700 (cloud-itonami-isic-0311 Marine fishing -- direct domain analog / reference)"
              "ADR-2607011000 (ISIC section coverage)"
              "cloud-itonami-isic-0312 repo docs/adr/0001-architecture.md"]

 :adr/context
 "cloud-itonami-isic-0311 (Marine fishing, ADR-2607151700) established a verified,
  tested fishing-fleet operations coordination actor. This ADR extends coverage to
  ISIC Rev.5 0312 (Freshwater fishing) as a fresh scaffold (no prior repo/attempt).
  Freshwater fishing needs the same back-office coordination as marine fishing
  (catch-record/quota logging, maintenance scheduling, safety-concern escalation,
  supply ordering) but has no maritime-zone (EEZ) concept: a vessel operates on a
  single named inland water body (river/lake) under one jurisdiction's permit/quota
  regime, not a multi-zone allocation. :water-body replaces 0311's :flag-state field;
  quota-exceedance remains a single-permit, single-quota hard check with no per-zone
  split. Safety-critical small-craft domain: coordination-only, no vessel navigation/
  command, fishing-gear-operation, or catch-decision authority."

 :adr/decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0312 as a freshwater fishing-fleet back-office
  operations coordination actor, mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-0311's verified
  pattern exactly in shape:
  - freshwater-fishing.governor: independent compliance layer -- vessel/permit
    verification (:vessel-not-found / :vessel-inactive), effect-matches-op
    (:effect-mismatch), propose-only (:non-propose-effect), forbidden fields
    :vessel-id/:permit-number/:vessel-status (:forbidden-field), closed op
    allowlist {:log-catch-record :schedule-vessel-maintenance :flag-safety-concern
    :order-supplies} with :navigate-vessel/:command-vessel/:decide-catch
    permanently blocked (:blocked-operation, no human override), quota-exceedance
    hard block (:quota-exceedance, no zone split). Soft escalations:
    :flag-safety-concern always escalates (vessel-safety/water-level/weather);
    supply orders >= 10,000 cost escalate; confidence < 0.6 escalates.
  - freshwater-fishing.store: Store protocol + MemStore -- vessel lookup
    (:water-body replaces 0311's :flag-state), log-catch! (accrues :landed-kg),
    schedule-maintenance!, flag-safety-concern!, order-supply!, audit-log.
  - freshwater-fishing.llm-advisor: Advisor protocol + mock impl, no external
    calls, structurally cannot generate ops outside the closed allowlist.
  - freshwater-fishing.operation: langgraph-clj OperationActor StateGraph
    (intake -> advise -> govern -> decide -> finalize), one graph run = one
    auditable operation, checkpointed, correct g/compile-graph API.
  - freshwater-fishing.sim: demo driver.
  Scope invariant: no vessel navigation, no fishing-gear operation, no catch
  decisions, no vessel command -- vessel operator's exclusive human authority
  on the water, permanently, no override path."

 :adr/consequences
 {:positive ["cloud-itonami-isic-0312 (Freshwater fishing) now has a real, tested implementation matching cloud-itonami-isic-0311 and every other cloud-itonami ISIC actor"
             "EEZ/maritime-zone concept deliberately absent (:water-body instead of :flag-state, single-permit quota) -- freshwater-specific adaptation, not a mechanical marine copy"
             "Safety-critical discipline (coordination-only, no navigation/vessel-command/gear-operation/catch-decision authority) preserved identically to the marine reference"
             "Closed op allowlist and hard quota-exceedance block leave no human-override path for regulatory or authority-boundary violations"
             "Self-inflicted registry-wide mojibake corruption (Perl -0777 -pi one-liner mixing raw-byte reads with a Unicode-escaped replacement) was caught immediately (anomalous diff size) and fixed same-session via an exact, automatic Python latin-1/utf-8 round-trip revert -- no manual transcription, no data loss, verified byte-identical to the last known-good commit outside the intended 0312 change"]
  :negative ["freshwater-fishing.sim's demo prints a summary rather than driving a full request through the compiled freshwater-fishing.operation graph end-to-end (mirrors 0311's own scope)"
             "No jurisdiction-specific regulatory-fact catalog (citation-backed facts.cljc) implemented; docs explicitly flag this as unimplemented"
             "The corruption briefly landed on kotoba-lang/industry's main (commits 0c00a63..1dd961a) before the fix merged -- a real regression this ADR's own author caused; future automated in-place edits to non-ASCII .edn files must use a tool with well-defined UTF-8 handling (this codebase's Edit tool, or Python 3 with explicit encoding=\"utf-8\"), never a raw Perl one-liner mixing byte-mode reads with Unicode-escaped replacement text"]}

 :adr/incident
 {:what "Automated retry-loop script's Perl -0777 -pi one-liner corrupted 859 pre-existing lines of kotoba-lang/industry's registry.edn (double-UTF-8-encoding mojibake, e.g. turnstile U+22A3 became garbled 'a-circumflex + pound-sign') while re-landing the 0312 registry edit across concurrent-agent 409 retries"
  :cause "Replacement text used a Perl Unicode escape (\\x{22a3}) without use utf8/encoding IO directives; Perl's byte-string/utf8-string upgrade semantics re-encoded every pre-existing multi-byte UTF-8 character in the whole file as if each original byte were a separate Latin-1 codepoint"
  :scope "859 lines in resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn; the newly-added cloud-itonami-isic-0312 entry itself was unaffected (used a real Perl Unicode literal, not raw file bytes)"
  :detected-by "Anomalous diff size on the merge commit (881 insertions/866 deletions for an intended ~20-line change) caught immediately after merge, before any other agent landed on top of it"
  :fixed-by "Python 3 script: line.encode('latin-1').decode('utf-8') per line -- succeeds only for corrupted lines (genuine non-Latin-1 codepoints, incl. the correct 0312 entry's own turnstile, raise UnicodeEncodeError and are left untouched), giving an exact automatic revert"
  :corrupting-commit "a78decb (merged 0c00a63)"
  :fix-commit "046d0ee (merged 1dd961a)"
  :verified "diff against last known-good pre-corruption commit d822e0d shows only the intended 20-line 0312 change; fresh clone shows zero mojibake occurrences and green test suite"}

